<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RM_TheForge_Biome.xml                      THEFORGE_RM_MOD_BUILD_1

    Phase A row 21 of design/RimMandrake/biome_mod_architecture.md — the
    RimMandrake-tier twin of the frozen src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/
    BiomeDefs/RUT_TheForge.xml, generalized to zero campaign-specific content
    per §3a's test. Full sheet (campaign-side):
    design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_forge.md (FROZEN).

    Copied from the frozen def, MEASURED 2026-09-25: diseases, terrain
    thresholds, animalDensity/plantDensity/forageability/movementDifficulty/
    diseaseMtbDays/wildPlantRegrowDays are all byte-identical to
    RUT_TheForge.xml's own values — nothing here is re-derived except the
    three fields the item's own analysis flagged as owing a change:

      - workerClass: the frozen twin's AlphaBiomes.BiomeWorker_PyroclasticConflagration
        is a donor type, which the RimMandrake tier may not assume as a hard
        dependency. Own RM_BiomeWorker_TheForge (Source/
        RM_BiomeWorker_TheForge.cs), scored from the massif's own MEASURED
        stats (the_forge.md §0: temps 42-56 C, elevation median 1,382-2,010 m,
        max 2,266 m) so RM_TheForge can also generate naturally on any OTHER
        player's world, the same shape as RM_BiomeWorker_TheRot.

      - texture: the frozen twin's "Biomes/AB_PyroclasticConflagration" is an
        Alpha Biomes donor texture. Reused vanilla Core's own
        "World/Biomes/ExtremeDesert" instead — same placeholder choice
        FloodedCanyon/Wasteland/Pyrelands already make for a hot/arid RM_
        biome with no closer vanilla equivalent (no lava/volcanic world
        texture ships in vanilla Core) — not invented art, a documented
        stand-in.

      - foragedFood: the frozen twin's "AB_RawBrownBarrelCactus" is an Alpha
        Biomes donor-only ThingDef. Reused vanilla "RawAgave" instead — the
        same vanilla-safe substitute Abyss/FloodedCanyon/Pyrelands
        already use for a hot/arid RM_ biome's foraging.

    terrainsByFertility keeps the frozen twin's three AB_ terrain bands
    inline, unguarded — RM_FloodedCanyon_Biome.xml already sets this exact
    precedent (AB_FineForsakenSand inline, no MayRequire) for a donor terrain
    family in an RM_-tier def; terrainsByFertility's own <li> does not carry
    a MayRequire field in the engine anyway.

    wildAnimals: every RSW_/SW_/donor-Star-Wars-name entry stays OUT (per
    §7 Q11, "RimMandrake should not name star wars ever") and rides
    src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/WildAnimals_TheForge.xml instead —
    casting the OWNED RSW_LavaFlea/RSW_Beldon ports rather than the donor's
    bare LavaFlea/Beldon defNames the frozen twin uses, which also fixes a
    latent defName mismatch: FORGE_MECHANICS_1's own tibanna-tap patch
    (RUT_TibannaTap_BeldonWiring.xml) has always targeted RSW_Beldon, a
    defName that has never actually spawned on the frozen RUT_TheForge (its
    own wildAnimals spawns only the donor's bare Beldon). This mod is the
    first place the tap's real target actually lives in a Forge wildAnimals
    list. Inline here: the 4 non-Star-Wars donor rows the frozen def already
    carries (Q9), AA_ColossalAerofleet (FORGE_RULED_CONTENT_1), RM_FleetFlier
    (COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1's own from-scratch, zero-donor creature) and
    the four ruled natives RM_Dhokkur/RM_Julmox/RM_Jossur/RM_Dhuvvox
    (FORGE_RULED_CONTENT_1).

    wildPlants: the frozen def's RUT_FireLavender/RUT_HeatsinkFungus are
    renamed RM_FireLavender/RM_HeatsinkFungus (§7 Q8's "each plant moves into
    the RimMandrake mod... renamed RM_", applied one biome sitting late).
    RUT_Sagecrust is NOT renamed to RM_Sagecrust here — that defName is
    already claimed by THEROT_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 for the SAME shared donor plant
    (RUT_Sagecrust is wired into both RUT_TheRot.xml and RUT_TheForge.xml).
    Per biome_mod_architecture.md §7 Q13 ("content wired into TWO biome
    mods: DUPLICATE, THEN DIVERGE... each mod carries its own copy under its
    own defName"), this biome's copy is RM_CinderCrust — same mechanical
    shape, a distinct identity, and no art yet (Q13's "regenerated" art half
    is separate, unowed work). See Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/RM_TheForge_Flora.xml
    for the full reasoning.

    biomeMapConditions/baseWeatherCommonalities: FORGE_MECHANICS_1's F1
    weather-pulse cycle (RM_ForgeStill/RM_BoilingRain/RM_ForgePulse) is
    authored natively in this mod (Defs/WeatherDefs/, Defs/GameConditionDefs/)
    rather than left as a second PatchOperationAdd op — the original patch
    (RUT_ForgePulse_BiomeWiring.xml) existed only because RUT_ForgePulse is a
    MayRequire-gated def that could dangle if injected directly into an
    always-loaded BiomeDef; here the condition ships IN this mod, so a
    direct <biomeMapConditions> reference cannot dangle. The frozen twin's
    RSW_SW_RedFog baseWeatherCommonalities entry is replaced with this mod's
    own RM_RedFog (owner ruling 2026-09-24, "make our own version and drop
    the SW label... it came from Alpha Biomes" - see RM_RedFog.xml's own
    header) at the same commonality (8).

    NOT this pass's scope, per this item's own §6/§9: the tibanna gas item
    and gather mechanism (F2, campaign plot - TIBANNA_EMBARGO_PLOT_1), the
    vapor-column ThinkTree wiring (F3, placeholder-only today), the foundry
    tower dungeon shell (F4, campaign plot), the Contagion die-off ring (F5,
    campaign lore), and the vent-industry buildings RUT_VentSmelter/VentForge/
    VentKiln (F6 - XML-only, freestanding production buildings with no
    BiomeDef field reference, left for FORGE_MECHANICS_1's own remaining
    move/rename pass rather than folded into this build). All are unaffected
    by this split; none blocks it.
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RM_TheForge</defName>
    <label>the Forge</label>
    <description>One mountain, three zones, and the only vertical skyline for a hundred kilometres: tall, dark foundry towers rising defiantly against the sun, streaming vent-steam like banners. Below them the red seams and the flows; around them the ash skirts; above them, improbably, herds -- vast placid gas-grazers drifting in the vapor columns. The mountain rains on itself in scalding bursts, and mosses drink in the seconds between fall and flash.</description>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.TheForge.RM_BiomeWorker_TheForge</workerClass>
    <texture>World/Biomes/ExtremeDesert</texture>
    <foragedFood>RawAgave</foragedFood>
    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>false</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>true</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>1.2</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.4</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.5</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1.5</movementDifficulty>
    <diseaseMtbDays>65</diseaseMtbDays>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.TheForge.RM_TheForgeBiomeRanges" />
      <!-- SOLAR_HEAT_EXPOSURE_1: sun heat kind "ambient" - the Forge: the_forge.md "one volcanic massif", "lava ... in scalding bursts".
           heatOffsetC is an invented first value; the owner-watched sitting tunes it. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_SunHeatExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">
        <heatKind>ambient</heatKind>
        <heatOffsetC>15</heatOffsetC>
      </li>
      <!-- BIOME_ARRIVAL_LETTERS_ALL_1 (DESIGN_PASS X-6/FV-5): PLACEHOLDER text drafted by an agent from this biome's
           own description, always-true list and shipped mechanics, flagged for the owner's review
           (infrastructure/state/items/BIOME_ARRIVAL_LETTERS_ALL_1.md). RM tier: plain reads, no narrator. Heat line follows heatKind. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_BiomeArrivalLetterExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">
        <letterLabel>The Forge</letterLabel>
        <letterText>The mountain runs on a cycle of fire and water, and the warning comes before each turn. Rain here falls boiling. Gas washes down and catches. Lava cools into a crust you can walk, until the melt comes back and takes whatever stands on it. The heat is in the air and the steam: shade does nothing here, so dress against it or stay in a closed room.</letterText>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>AB_BlackPebbles</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.7</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>AB_HardenedGrass</terrain>
        <min>0.7</min>
        <max>0.9</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>AB_HardenedGrassFertile</terrain>
        <min>0.9</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <!-- FORGE_LAVA_TERRAIN_1: open lava at map generation. Owner-typed design
         authority: "The open lava is horrible, hot, deadly." The Forge cycle
         (RM_ForgePulse's freezableTerrains) crusts and melts LavaDeep only, so
         this is the terrain laid here. Mechanism is vanilla Odyssey's own:
         LavaField's BiomeDef uses exactly this terrainPatchMakers shape
         (Perlin 0.035/1.5/6, LavaDeep above 0.9, VolcanicRock rim).
         GenStep_Terrain -> MapGenUtility.TerrainFrom applies patch makers
         before rock/gravel/fertility bands and destroys any rock edifice on a
         cell whose terrain has supportsRock=false, so lava cuts through the
         massif as it does on a vanilla lava field. Heat, ignition and burns
         are TerrainDef-driven (SteadyEnvironmentEffects heatPerTick,
         HediffGiver_Terrain burnDamage/ignitePawnsIntervalTicks) - no GenStep
         or MapComponent is needed. isPond is false on purpose: a
         preventsPondGeneration mutator must not erase the Forge's lava.
         Coverage (offline Perlin approximation, 12 seeds on a 250x250 map):
         ~9% LavaDeep (range ~5.5-14%) plus ~5% walkable CooledLava banks;
         vanilla LavaField's 0.9 threshold gives ~2%. -->
    <terrainPatchMakers>
      <!-- Lava fields: pools and lakes of open lava, CooledLava shore. -->
      <li>
        <perlinFrequency>0.035</perlinFrequency>
        <perlinLacunarity>1.5</perlinLacunarity>
        <perlinOctaves>6</perlinOctaves>
        <isPond>false</isPond>
        <thresholds>
          <li>
            <terrain>CooledLava</terrain>
            <min>0.55</min>
            <max>0.7</max>
          </li>
          <li>
            <terrain>LavaDeep</terrain>
            <min>0.7</min>
            <max>999</max>
          </li>
        </thresholds>
      </li>
      <!-- Lava seams: a thin band around zero of a low-frequency Perlin traces
           winding contour lines - rivers of lava. Gated to fertility <= 0.65
           so the seams break over the fertile ground: impassable lava must
           never cut the map into sealed pieces, and the gaps are the crossings. -->
      <li>
        <perlinFrequency>0.012</perlinFrequency>
        <perlinLacunarity>2</perlinLacunarity>
        <perlinOctaves>4</perlinOctaves>
        <maxFertility>0.65</maxFertility>
        <isPond>false</isPond>
        <thresholds>
          <li>
            <terrain>LavaDeep</terrain>
            <min>-0.025</min>
            <max>0.025</max>
          </li>
          <li>
            <terrain>CooledLava</terrain>
            <min>-0.045</min>
            <max>0.045</max>
          </li>
        </thresholds>
      </li>
    </terrainPatchMakers>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>40</Clear>
      <AB_VolcanicAsh MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">20</AB_VolcanicAsh>
      <AB_VolcanicAshRain MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">6</AB_VolcanicAshRain>
      <RM_RedFog>8</RM_RedFog>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <biomeMapConditions>
      <li>RM_ForgePulse</li>
    </biomeMapConditions>
    <wildAnimals>
      <AA_Aerofleet MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.4</AA_Aerofleet>  <!-- aerofleet - sky -->
      <LavaSnail MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">0.35</LavaSnail>  <!-- lava snail - ground-slow -->
      <AA_Metallovore MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.15</AA_Metallovore>  <!-- metallovore - ground-slow -->
      <AA_CrescendoAnole MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.5</AA_CrescendoAnole>  <!-- crescendo anole - small, ECOSYSTEM_PYRAMID_LAW_1 -->
      <RM_FleetFlier>0.45</RM_FleetFlier>  <!-- fleet flier - small sky, from-scratch, renamed from RUT_FleetFlier -->
      <!-- FORGE_RULED_CONTENT_1 (FORGE_BEDAZZLE_SITTING_1, owner turn 2 "Wire in all
           waiting."): the roster's AA_ColossalAerofleet row, weight from
           rosters/the_forge.json. -->
      <AA_ColossalAerofleet MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.5</AA_ColossalAerofleet>  <!-- greater bulloo - sky, LARGE -->
      <!-- FORGE_RULED_CONTENT_1 (turn 4 "1) admit."): the four admitted natives,
           Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RM_TheForgeNatives.xml. The dhuvvox's baseline row
           spawns them; FORGE_CYCLE_MECHANICS_1's dormancy comp seals the
           dhokkur/julmox/dhuvvox between rains. Mass dhuvvox eruption at a
           burst is a later tranche. -->
      <RM_Dhokkur>0.02</RM_Dhokkur>  <!-- dhokkur - GIANT, rain-drinker -->
      <RM_Julmox>0.4</RM_Julmox>  <!-- julmox - ground herd, tamable -->
      <RM_Jossur>0.06</RM_Jossur>  <!-- jossur - sky apex predator -->
      <RM_Dhuvvox>0.3</RM_Dhuvvox>  <!-- dhuvvox - flash-swarm, small -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <Plant_Fireweed>0.9</Plant_Fireweed>  <!-- fireweed -->
      <Plant_MagmaCactus>0.7</Plant_MagmaCactus>  <!-- magma cactus -->
      <RM_FireLavender>0.6</RM_FireLavender>  <!-- renamed from RUT_FireLavender -->
      <RM_CinderCrust>0.4</RM_CinderCrust>  <!-- this biome's own variant of the shared crust-fungus, §7 Q13 -->
      <IronScruff_PrimordialGrass MayRequire="IronScruff.PrimordialGeysers">0.35</IronScruff_PrimordialGrass>  <!-- primordial grass -->
      <AB_TinkleGrass MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">0.3</AB_TinkleGrass>  <!-- tinkle grass -->
      <IronScruff_PrimordialTallGrass MayRequire="IronScruff.PrimordialGeysers">0.3</IronScruff_PrimordialTallGrass>  <!-- primordial tall grass -->
      <IronScruff_Bindweed MayRequire="IronScruff.PrimordialGeysers">0.25</IronScruff_Bindweed>  <!-- bindweed -->
      <AB_FirevineTree MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">0.2</AB_FirevineTree>  <!-- firevine tree - tree -->
      <RM_HeatsinkFungus>0.2</RM_HeatsinkFungus>  <!-- renamed from RUT_HeatsinkFungus, tree -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>27</wildPlantRegrowDays>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
